NNAAMMEE
     nnffssssttaatt — display NFS statistics

SSYYNNOOPPSSIISS
     nnffssssttaatt [--ccss] [--MM _c_o_r_e] [--NN _s_y_s_t_e_m] [--ww _w_a_i_t]

DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
     nnffssssttaatt displays statistics kept about NFS client and server activity.
     If neither --MM nor --NN option was specified, statistics will be obtained
     from the running system by calling sysctl(2).  Otherwise the specified
     core and system will be used to fetch data by means of kvm(3).

     The options are as follows:

     --cc      Display client statistics only.

     --MM _c_o_r_e
             Extract values associated with the name list from the specified
             core instead of the default _/_d_e_v_/_k_m_e_m.

     --NN _s_y_s_t_e_m
             Extract the name list from the specified system instead of the
             default _/_b_s_d.

     --ss      Display server statistics only.

     --ww _w_a_i_t
             Display a shorter summary of NFS activity for both the client and
             server at _w_a_i_t second intervals.

FFIILLEESS
     /bsd       default kernel namelist
     /dev/kmem  default memory file

SSEEEE AALLSSOO
     fstat(1), netstat(1), ps(1), systat(1), sysctl(2), kvm(3), iostat(8),
